{"ts": "2026-10-30T02:27:33.302521Z", "run_id": "r-20261030T0227Z-af38", "unit": "openspec:add-web-data-kit", "seq": 9, "type": "base.merged", "base": "main", "base_sha": "b01b0f04212ac950c71b741a895086a700ee0a56", "merge_sha": "8dee7a9ea41246ba3cd36b97bfe5ae777e98fc4c", "behind": 1, "resolved": [], "frozen_touched": []}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T02:27:33.334444Z", "run_id": "r-20261030T0227Z-af38", "unit": "openspec:add-web-data-kit", "seq": 10, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-034", "target": "H-da5c95d0", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "The hold may be waived. Criterion C-ab5cf141 is the fix's regression scenario \"Load more after an empty page unmounts the focused button\": the return values of tableView and focusAfterChange, pure functions in data-table.ts, which no page shows. The fix keys the busy Load more and the end-of-list focus on a non-null nextCursor, and its Node tests (C-686289b8 C-ab5cf141 tableView keeps a load more after an empty page busy; C-ab5cf141 focusAfterChange moves to the table) passed with a red assertion. design.md \"Browser coverage, stated plainly\" says no page uses these components and add-web-ui-kit rules out a kit demo route, so this unit has no journey; the first consumers (add-web-admin for DataTable, add-web-task-inbox for SchemaForm) prove the markup with assert_accessible(page).", "text_sha256": "f83b8a8806f7eab89211545e38ca815c76e53681b8adcd829fe1cc9393765fb6", "answer_sha256": "2c3272f28d626f9a9f018a02f03df0aa3a3a3955fe230c857935692d9f3124f8", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T02:27:33.335109Z", "run_id": "r-20261030T0227Z-af38", "unit": "openspec:add-web-data-kit", "seq": 11, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-035", "target": "H-b3bec5d6", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The hold may be waived. Criterion C-852bb719 is the fix unit's regression scenario \"An unsupported property c comes back with an empty name\": schemaToFields, given the schema of \"Unsupported properties\", labels the untyped property c as \"C\" with the reason \"the property has no type\" and leaves the other six fields unchanged. That is the return value of a pure function in schema-fields.ts, which no page shows: parseProperty keeps the label derived from the name and blanks only the name, and the Node test for the criterion asserts the seven names, the seven labels A to G, the seven reasons and the Unsupported prefix, and passed with a red assertion. No file of the web app outside web/src/kit/data imports SchemaForm or schemaToFields, so no route mounts the component, and the design's test plan and the proposal both state that this change has no kit demo route and no browser journey, leaving the markup to the first consumers add-web-task-inbox and add-web-admin. A browser test therefore c", "text_sha256": "1a65348f26911dc29eb6dea53986759bd82b214bf389427fd8a7a513f5e16dc3", "answer_sha256": "5b5ad96dd454a4fcca0dfbab43e9c2f25942db58e3969d7b615ce8c2f168f82a", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T02:27:33.343491Z", "run_id": "r-20261030T0227Z-af38", "unit": "openspec:add-web-data-kit", "seq": 12, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-036", "target": "H-d3c23a86", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "The hold may be waived. Criterion C-247ad9d2 is the regression scenario \"task 1.1: no-op calls and loads do not settle with the request in flight\": when the promises of load, loadMore and retry settle, an API timing no page shows. start now returns a promise that resolves once its request's outcome is committed or reset() drops it (cursor-list.ts finishPending), calls that start nothing still resolve at once, and its Node tests (C-247ad9d2 load loadMore and retry settle with their request; C-efc9d8f0 C-247ad9d2 no-op calls settle at once while a request is in flight) passed with a red assertion. design.md \"Browser coverage, stated plainly\" says no page uses these components and add-web-ui-kit rules out a kit demo route, so this unit has no journey; the first consumers (add-web-admin for DataTable, add-web-task-inbox for SchemaForm) prove the markup with assert_accessible(page).", "text_sha256": "6631bf7536a3818db71616f2f44b3bd339b5323becae1517050c2c308f9b7b76", "answer_sha256": "9f1f532dbe8e4ad50a4f3f1201fcf039bb93f63100c5e326cf2fbe56f91df4e8", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
{"ts": "2026-10-30T02:27:33.351936Z", "run_id": "r-20261030T0227Z-af38", "unit": "openspec:add-web-data-kit", "seq": 13, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-037", "target": "H-e860473b", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "The hold may be waived. Criterion C-a0904f4d is the scenario of finding F-d49cb373 \"task 4.1: an enum property without type is not rendered as an enum\": the return value of schemaToFields, which no page shows. parseProperty now makes a property with its own enum and no type an enum field, a property with neither keeps the reason \"the property has no type\", and its Node test (C-a0904f4d schemaToFields treats an enum without type as a text enum) passed with a red assertion. design.md \"Browser coverage, stated plainly\" says no page uses these components and add-web-ui-kit rules out a kit demo route, so this unit has no journey; the first consumers (add-web-admin for DataTable, add-web-task-inbox for SchemaForm) prove the markup with assert_accessible(page).", "text_sha256": "42731c08b9cc121741c8ed6c0fc0a3032ecb06807960c00eba4d896a50f260be", "answer_sha256": "789c6947058fff1ab3993672383670d10fd4860ea80ff1a8e429399477776c0f", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
